0 23 591 [
[(Pure Data offers a "data structure" feature that allows you)]
[(to visualize quantitative data, such as a musical score, in)]
[(a way that freely reflects your own visual design. Objects)]
[(in Pd allow you to access and/or modify the data - for)]
[(example, you could make a visualized audio analysis of an)]
[(incoming sound, edit it, and then use the result to control)]
[(a synthesizer.)]
] 14 -0 0 0 false DrawText
grestore
gsave
/Menlo-Regular findfont 12 scalefont ISOEncode setfont
0.000 0.000 0.000 setrgbcolor AdjustColor
0 23 335 [
[(In this series of example patches you'll see the central)]
[(idea behind Pure Data - not to make a Max-like program, but)]
[(rather to make data visible and audible for musical)]
[(purposes. \050But the Max stuff is necessary infrastructure and)]
[(to use the features shown here you will need to understand)]
[(the control and audio examples as well as this "data)]
[(structures" series.\051)]
] 14 -0 0 0 false DrawText
grestore
gsave
/Menlo-Regular findfont 12 scalefont ISOEncode setfont
0.000 0.000 0.000 setrgbcolor AdjustColor
0 23 478 [
[(The Pure Data features shown here are meant as a response to)]
[(a dream shared by electronic musicians since the early days)]
[(of audio synthesis: to be able to treat sound quality)]
[(\050"timbre"\051 as a musical element that could be specified,)]
[(controlled, and in general used for music composition in the)]
[(same way as pitch and rhythm have long been. To make sound)]
[(visible and editable is a grandiose project and we can't)]
[(claim to have realized it yet - this is an unfinished)]
[(project.)]
] 14 -0 0 0 false DrawText
grestore
gsave
/Menlo-Regular findfont 12 scalefont ISOEncode setfont
0.000 0.000 0.000 setrgbcolor AdjustColor
0 24 224 [
[(The objects to the right, called "scalars", are members of a)]
[(data type \050a "structure"\051 that is defined in the)]
[("how-it-works" window below. With the patch in run mode you)]
[(can click on the displayed numbers \050five for each of the)]
[(objects\051 to alter them, or you can click on the hot point)]
[(shown as a small black square to move it around. In edit)]
[(mode you can select, move, or copy/paste the objects.)]
] 14 -0 0 0 false DrawText
grestore
gsave
/Menlo-Regular findfont 12 scalefont ISOEncode setfont
0.000 0.000 0.000 setrgbcolor AdjustColor
0 198 107 [
[(Everything is defined in a subwindow;)]
[(you can click here and see --->)]
] 14 -0 0 0 false DrawText
